["<task-notification>\n<task-id>a575220c40aff06cd</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01XhyjbVmVNuxyZmkqCnHw3s</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/a575220c40aff06cd.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Progression: equipment system\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The equipment feature is done and committed in three commits on `feature/equipment`. All 388 EditMode tests pass (39 of them new), and the headless bot completes its runs with the equipment module installed. Not merged, rebased or pushed.\n\n## Design\n- **Player slots (4):** weapon, off-hand, armor and one trinket. I kept one trinket rather than two: a run is only about 5 rooms, and a second trinket mostly doubles numbers without adding a new choice. Adding one later is an enum entry.\n- **Companion slot (1):** a companion focus whose stats go to the companion's own stat sheet.\n- **Content:** 18 base types, 17 affixes, 3 uniques, 4 rarities (普通/精良/稀有/传说). All text is Chinese with no special glyphs.\n- **Uniques:** each has a behaviour hooked through GameEvents:\n  - 宿敌之牙: heal 4 on every kill.\n  - 荆棘回响: 15 damage to the nearest enemy when you are hit.\n  - 残影坠饰: +25% damage for 3 s after dodging a nemesis move.\n- **Generator:** `GearGenerator.Generate(seed, ctx)` gives the same item for the same seed and context.\n  - Base odds are 60/28/10/2. Luck and nemesis tier raise the better rarities.\n  - Boss drops are never Common.\n  - Item level 1–10 scales affix values up to ×1.54.\n  - \"Boss tier\" didn't exist anywhere, so I defined it as the number of previous wins, capped at 5.\n- **Balance:** realistic end-game gear gives about +45–60% damage, below Meta's +75%. Salvage pays 1/2/3/6 shards.\n- **Getting gear:**\n  - Each cleared combat room has a 35% drop chance, and every run is guaranteed at least one drop. If you walk past it, the companion picks it up.\n  - Beating the boss saves a choose-1-of-3 reward. The result screen shows a notice, and the choice opens as a modal when you return to the Hub.\n  - The Hub panel opens with E. It shows the slots, the stash, current vs selected, and how the final stats would change (green better, red worse). It handles equip, unequip and salvage (press X twice), and works with the mouse too.\n- **Persistence:** gear survives across runs in a new `SaveData.equipment` field. Old saves load and get the starter kit, which matches the knight's old look.\n\nFull reasoning is in `docs/specs/equipment.md`.\n\n## Changes outside my folders (the lead needs to know)\n- **`Player.cs`:** a `WeaponProfile Weapon` field and `Reach`/`HalfAngle` properties. Both attack lookups now use them, and the attack's wind-up/recovery is scaled by the weapon. The default profile leaves the attack exactly as before.\n- **`VfxDirector.cs` and `DebugOverlay.cs`:** both now draw the attack fan from the live reach/angle, so the visual matches axes and daggers.\n- **`Companion.cs`:** one line, `public StatSheet Stats { get; } = BaseStats.ForCompanion();`. This will conflict with the stats branch; keep theirs.\n- **`ArtLibrary.cs`:** a new public `Rearm(...)` for re-dressing at runtime. Props attached earlier are now marked and removed on re-arm.\n- **`Data.cs`:** one field placed after `nextPlan`, not at the end of the class, to reduce merge conflicts with the other branches.\n- **Stat sources:** each slot is one source (`equip:weapon`, `equip:offhand`, `equip:armor`, `equip:trinket`; `equip:companion` on the companion's sheet), plus a temporary `equip:trinket:afterimage` for the 残影 buff. No new StatIds.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Tests:** 388/388 pass, including the 3 art tests, which ran rather than being skipped. Results are in `tests-equipment.xml` in the scratchpad.\n- **Headless bot (2 runs, no screenshots):** completed with `[BOT] finished runs=2 wins=2`.\n  - The log shows the loadout and weapon profile at each run start, a room drop picked up by the companion, the boss offer and the bot taking the first card.\n  - In the saved file, the ring from that offer was auto-equipped into the empty trinket slot.\n- **Screenshots:** IMGUI screenshots only work when Unity runs with a window, not with `-batchmode`. The first `-batchmode` attempt with screenshots froze in the Hub because of the existing HUD capture code, not mine. I then ran the bot windowed, with the window opening on the scratch copy.\n  - The panel, the two-handed blocked state, the unique trinket diff and the boss offer render cleanly at 720p and 1080p. The Hub \"E 装备\" button sits between the cards and the controls line without overlapping. The pickup toast and the result notice don't overlap the HUD.\n  - The first round showed two issues, both fixed and re-checked: text touching the slot-row borders, and duplicate stat lines like \"护甲 +2\" twice.\n- **Close-ups:**\n  - Axe + round shield: correct hands.\n  - Greatsword: left hand empty.\n  - Dagger + tower shield + leather: helmet hidden.\n  - Sword + spiked shield: correct.\n  - Companion with the tome: wand plus open spellbook.\n\n## Known limits\n- The staff (`Skeleton_Staff`) is not clearly visible in its close-ups. The art test confirms it is the only active item in the right hand, but it may be oriented oddly. The adventurers' own `staff` prop can't be used because `Art/Props` has no `mage_texture`.\n- Until the stats branch makes Player/Companion read their stat sheets, only the weapon profile and the unique effects change gameplay on this branch.\n- The game has no elites, so gear only drops from cleared rooms and the boss.\n- The drop marker's floor disc reads as a bright solid blob. I lowered its glow but didn't re-check it on screen.\n- The greatsword's floor drop shows the one-handed sword model, because no two-handed sword prop is imported.\n\n## Files\n- `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/equipment/unity/Assets/Scripts/Core/Equipment/` (`GearDefs.cs`, `Gear.cs`, `GearGenerator.cs`, `Loadout.cs`, `GearText.cs`)\n- `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/equipment/unity/Assets/Scripts/Game/Features/Equipment/` (`EquipmentModule.cs`, `EquipmentLayer.cs`, `EquipmentPanelModel.cs`, `EquipmentLook.cs`, `EquipmentEvents.cs`, `EquipmentShot.cs`)\n- `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/equipment/unity/Assets/Tests/Editor/EquipmentGeneratorTests.cs`, `EquipmentLoadoutTests.cs`, `EquipmentPanelTests.cs`\n- `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/equipment/docs/specs/equipment.md`\n- Screenshots: `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/scratchpad/equip-shots/`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>296735</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>40</tool_uses><duration_ms>1037786</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>", "<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab910a12c1e51d560</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_015hnRYw9gu1zDbSaFBq5vf1</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/ab910a12c1e51d560.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Progression: stats wiring and levels\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I've finished the stats task and committed it in two commits on `feature/stats`: 6963d19 (Core model and wiring) and 49b6519 (Growth feature module and spec). The EditMode tests pass and the bot completes its runs with the module installed. The UI screenshots were never captured, so I have not seen the HUD strip, the level-up toast or the C sheet on screen.\n\n**Design** (written up with the reasoning in `docs/specs/stats.md`):\n- **Player level resets every run.** Max HP and damage already grow permanently through Meta (up to +100 HP and +75% damage). A permanent player level on top would double up, and would let raw numbers beat the boss that learns your habits. A per-run level gives each run a clear curve, like Vampire Survivors.\n- **Player XP and growth:** grunt kills give 10 XP, archers 12, the boss 60. Levels come at 20, 50, 90, 140 total XP, up to level 10. Each level adds +8 max HP and +5% attack. A typical run reaches level 4 before the boss, which is roughly one Meta level.\n- **The companion's bond level is permanent**, in the spirit of Hades relationships. Bond XP comes from a quarter of all kill XP, +1 per bolt that hits, +10 per heal, +20 per finished run and +20 more for a win. Bond levels come at 100, 250, 450 total XP, up to level 10.\n- **Old companion behaviour is kept.** Bond level = max(old runs rule, bond XP level), so existing saves never drop. Level 2 still unlocks the heal and level 3 the 1.0s fire interval. Stat growth (+10% attack and heal per level) only starts at level 4, so numbers for current saves are unchanged.\n- **Abandoning a run** from the pause menu takes back the bond XP earned in it, consistent with \"abandon gives no rewards\".\n- **Combat formulas:** armor reduces damage by armor/(armor+50), capped at 60%, and a hit always does at least 1. Life steal is capped at 50%. Dash cooldown has a 0.4s floor, which the old 轻灵 boon floor now applies to every source.\n\n**Equivalence:** Meta and the boons now apply as sources `meta:hp`, `meta:dmg` and `boon:&lt;id&gt;`. Tests check every Meta level 0–5 against 0–3 picks of each boon and get the old numbers. They also check that boon rolls use the same random numbers as before. Picking a boon twice adds to one source, so the sheet shows \"利刃 +40%\".\n\n**One intended change:** the contract's 5% base crit chance is now live, so expected player damage is about 2.5% higher than before. Crits use their own RNG so boon rolls and spawns don't shift.\n\n**Verification:**\n- **EditMode tests:** 455 of 455 passed, 0 failed (baseline was 335 plus the StatSheet tests).\n- **Bot (2 runs):** finished with `[BOT] finished runs=2 wins=2`. The log shows `[LEVEL] player Lv2…Lv5`, `[LEVEL] companion bond Lv2 xp=100` and `[GROWTH] run end player Lv5 xp=164 crits=2 | companion bond Lv2 xp=192`. Log: `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/scratchpad/bot-stats-ok.log`.\n- **Bot stalls:** two earlier bot attempts stopped making progress partway, both times right after a `TrimDiskCacheJob` log line. The editor loop was still running and no script was looping. I can't rule out my changes, but this matches the known headless Unity issue. That passing run also had a temporary diagnostic line added in the scratch copy only, not committed.\n- **Screenshots: not captured.** Neither growth-shot attempt got past the Hub. The bot's own first HUD capture never finished, because Unity never repainted the IMGUI layer in this session. Only the camera-only `1-hub.png` was written. The capture tool I added (`AGENT_GROWTH_SHOT=1`, see spec section 8) needs a session where IMGUI repaints, e.g. with the display awake.\n- Every run used `AGENT_SAVE` scratch files, and I added nothing that writes settings.\n\n**What the lead needs for merging:**\n- **Edits outside my folders:**\n  - `Stats.cs` `ForPlayer`: base max HP comes from `Meta.BaseHp` plus the meta sources, the player gets `SkillPower = 1`, and `PickupRange` changed from 2.5 to 3.5 to match the existing magnet radius. Final values are unchanged and the existing StatSheet test still passes.\n  - `Data.cs`: one field at the end, `growth`. Old saves load with defaults.\n  - `CommonEvents.cs`: a new `CritHit` event.\n  - `Projectile.Friendly`: an optional `onHit` callback.\n  - `DamageNumber`: a text overload, used for the \"CRIT!\" marker.\n  - Pickups feature: a `PickupMagnet.Speed(d, radius)` overload, and one changed line in `PickupsModule.cs`.\n- **Removed:** `Player.speedMul`, `dmgMul`, `dashCdMax` and `companionMul`. Any branch still reading them won't compile. Use `Player.Stats` and `Player.DashCooldownMax`.\n- **`Player.maxHp`** is now a mirror of the MaxHp stat; don't write it directly. Any `SetSource` that raises MaxHp also heals by the raise.\n- **For talents/items/equipment:** call `ctx.Player.Stats.SetSource(...)` or `ctx.Companion.Stats.SetSource(...)`. The sheet lists any source id; `talent:`, `item:` and `equip:` get a Chinese prefix. Friendly names can be passed through `nameOf` in `CharacterSheetLayer.NameOf`.\n- **No new `StatId` values.** Luck is still unused.\n\n**Limits:**\n- The C sheet doesn't pause the game.\n- The \"CRIT!\" marker is English because the built-in damage-number font has no Chinese, and it appears on top of the normal yellow number rather than replacing it.\n\nFiles are in `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/stats/unity/Assets/`:\n- Scripts/Core/Growth/Leveling.cs\n- Scripts/Core/Growth/CombatRules.cs\n- Scripts/Core/Growth/CharacterSheet.cs\n- Scripts/Game/Features/Growth/GrowthModule.cs\n- Scripts/Game/Features/Growth/GrowthLayers.cs\n- Scripts/Game/Features/Growth/GrowthShot.cs\n- Scripts/Game/Features/Growth/GrowthEvents.cs\n- Tests/Editor/StatsMigrationTests.cs\n- Tests/Editor/StatsGrowthTests.cs\n\nThe spec is `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/stats/docs/specs/stats.md`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>242589</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>32</tool_uses><duration_ms>2183159</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"]
